Usage with Different Formats
python# Parquet
df.write.mode("overwrite").parquet("/output/path")

# CSV
df.write.mode("append").option("header", True).csv("/output/path")

# JSON
df.write.mode("overwrite").json("/output/path")

# Delta Lake
df.write.mode("overwrite").format("delta").save("/output/path")

# JDBC (database)
df.write.mode("append").jdbc(url, table, properties)

# Saving as a table
df.write.mode("overwrite").saveAsTable("my_table")

Using SaveMode Enum (Java/Scala style in PySpark)
pythonfrom pyspark.sql import SaveMode

df.write.mode(SaveMode.Overwrite).parquet("/path")
